{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1396770-lock-effects","id":1396770,"title":"Lock Effects","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Mage: The Ascension"],"posts":[{"date":"2020-06-15T18:20:52-07:00","id":1396770,"title":"Lock Effects","content":"Hello there, I know that Magick doesn't move with the target and if you need the spell keep going with it you need to Lock-In effect with the proper sphere related to the pattern (Matter,Life,Life[+]).<br /> But there's some things I can't understand about this rule, that rule applies how exactly? If you cast a curse in someone that rule applies? I remember old routines like Death Curse[?], I can't remember exact name but it's from Spirit Ways or Dreamspeakers book (Spirit 3 and Entropy 3). In this case you're locking in the target spirit so you don't need life? You could also for example lock effects on your or someone else subconscious with Mind? With Prime you can lock effect on youself?<br /> There's another subject that makes me a little confused too, about Time-Trigger Effects, for example, if I want to cast a dream spell to carry with me but without a target subject decided at the casting, generally the difficult is WP for Sleepers, +3 to Nightfolks, and +5 to elder vampires or with dominate, okay, maybe it's reasonable to say that you set the difficult level based on the target max WP your spell will affect? For example, if you AIM to target Sleeper up to 8 WP and Nightfolk/mages up to 5 WP you roll the cast set at 8 dif, that is correct and possible?<br /> And a last question about threshold rule, if the difficult of a ritual is set to 9 + 3 for a single sucess you have to reach this goal at each roll? Or you need to gather at least 3 sucess to pass the threshold and then proceed at difficult 9?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":26165,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26165-gothicxxx","user":"GothicxXx","date":". 06-15-2020, 09:46 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26165-gothicxxx","name":"GothicxXx","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26165_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-15T23:27:37-07:00","id":1396826,"title":"","content":"Okay, first the topic of locking a spell:<br /> <br /> You wouldn't need it for a curse, no, since Entropy 4 directly allows you to affect living things with such an effect (See the Entropy 4 description).<br /> The golden rule of locking on an effect is: You need to do it whenever <i>you want to use a sphere on a Pattern (Living thing, matter, forces, a spirit etc.), but the sphere's effects do not directly relate to such a pattern, normally.</i><br /> The example in M20 is a good one, where if you create an invisibility field on another person, The field would normally stay in the very spot you created it. The Forces sphere can create an invisibility field by bending light, but the Forces sphere has nothing to do with the pattern of said person. Now, your Mage could move that field actively with concentration to keep it on the person as they walk and move about - but this would make the spell count against the &quot;+1 difficulty increase for every two running spells that demand concentration&quot;.<br /> The alternative? Lock on the effect (i.e. the invisibility field) onto the other person's Life pattern so the field automagically moves with them. Hence you addd Life to the Forces effect.<br /> <br /> It's not just about location though - in general, locking on is required if you wish to affect a Pattern with a different sphere that normally does not relate to that pattern. Say, transform a living thing into a statue - which would be Life + Matter.<br /> <br /> <br /> As for your example of a time-hung mind effect without a specified target, and guessing ahead the difficulty of the roll - you are pretty much correct, yes.<br /> The Arete roll you need to do ahead of time essentially needs to be done at the same difficulty as if it had been cast in-the-moment. So, in case of a Mind spell you kind of need to guess and take a gamble regarding the difficulty to roll it at, as that determines the chance of it actually being able to affect a certain target later.<br /> <br /> <br /> Regarding the threshold rule - if the difficulty of a RItual would go over 9, you'd need to breach that threshold with every roll, AFAIK. And damn, that would be one tough ritual if the difficulty goes over 9. Large rituals in general are best performed with a healthy stockpile of Quintessence at hand to lower difficulties.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://is.gd/wodchart\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Probability Chart</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodcalc\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Statistics Calculator</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodarmor\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Armor System</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Damage Roll System</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage2\" target=\"_blank\">My explanation of cWoD Damage Levels</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodstrength\" target=\"_blank\">'Interesting' Strength Attribute Stuff</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodboom\" target=\"_blank\">EXPLOSIVE cWoD STUFF!</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodheresy\" target=\"_blank\">How Technocrats don't think they are Mages</a>","edited":{"userid":6606,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6606-ambrosia","user":"Ambrosia","date":". 06-17-2020, 08:31 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6606-ambrosia","name":"Ambrosia","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/